Z||000002||Old Lar||01-21-2001||01:04 PM||||Ebay seems to hve too many rip off sellers out here.  If you are in the market for some item and have to have it, you can pay as much as you want.  And some fool may pay some exhorbitant price for a Fiero wing or other specialty part.<P>I won't bid on anything without a posted reserve.  If some one wants $10000 for a $1000 item, I want to know upfront, so I don't waste my time.  My $0.02, reserve not met.||||reg||13
Z||000003||Songman||01-21-2001||01:10 PM||||That's a good idea, Lar... I have only had one auction with a reserve price and that was for an perfect endura front bumper for a 69 GTO with hideaway headlights. I had a $500 reserve on it and had a lot of e-mails asking what the reserve was. I should have just posted it in the auction. I will if I ever have another reserve auction.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
